! ----------------------------------------------------------
! Basis set: pob-tzvp ECPs
! Effective core potentials carried by the pob-TZVP records for Rb-I
! (CRYSTAL Z+200 convention), converted from the Bredow-group per-element
! sources in python/vibeqc/basis_library/sources/pob-TZVP/ by
! vibeqc.basis_crystal.emit_ecp_sidecar. The channels are exactly the
! primitive arrays vibeqc.basis_crystal.crystal_ecp_to_libecpint_arrays
! feeds libecpint on the periodic route, so molecular and periodic runs use
! one ECP.
! Originating publication: J. Laun, D. Vilela Oliveira, T. Bredow,
!   J. Comput. Chem. 39, 1285 (2018); DOI: 10.1002/jcc.25195
! ECP parameters: Stuttgart-Cologne energy-consistent pseudopotentials as
!   distributed with the pob-TZVP Rb-I basis; the same potentials as the
!   pob-TZVP-rev2 Rb-I records (per-element references: Leininger 1996 Rb,
!   Kaupp 1991 Sr, Andrae 1990 Y-Cd, Metz 2000 In-Sb, Peterson 2003 Te-I).
! Source URL: https://www.chemie.uni-bonn.de/bredow/de/software/pob-tzvp-rb-i-tar.gz
!   (pob-TZVP-Rb-I.tar.gz, 7280 bytes, sha256 2b341b8f0169548b2904e9db27dc0d9e
!   be86ee1eede0a8c0ed2225d434bf194e), retrieved 2026-09-13
! License: bundled with the Bredow group's agreement (docs/license.md 3a)
! ----------------------------------------------------------
!
